{
    "background_story": "Kayden was a free-spirited artist, often lost in his own creative world. His obliviousness to the world around him was both a blessing and a curse. He would spend hours painting, completely unaware of the time, his surroundings, or even his own hunger. His friends and family had grown accustomed to his absent-mindedness, often laughing at his forgetfulness. One day, while working on a new masterpiece, Kayden failed to notice a severe storm warning. As the storm rolled in, he continued to paint, oblivious to the howling wind and pouring rain. It wasn't until the power went out that he finally looked up, startled, and wondered what all the fuss was about. Despite his obliviousness, Kayden's art was a reflection of his unique perspective, and his carefree nature made him a beloved fixture in the community.",
